I want to hang my keys by the door.
But where are my keys?
I ask Nina.
"Where are my keys?"
I look on the table.
They are not on the table.
I go into the kitchen.
Are they in the kitchen?
No, they are not here.
Nina helps me.
She looks too.
"Are they in your bag?" she asks.
I look in my bag.
No, they are not in the bag either.
